<div class="page-head">
  <div class="dotgrid" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Our story</span>
    <h1 style="margin-top:10px">{{ page.title | default: 'Why we built KeepKase' }}</h1>
    <p class="dek">A case that protects the laptop — and a way to keep the things you put on it.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="story-block">
  <div class="story-grid">
    <div class="story-media bg-blue"><div class="placeholder-media" style="height:100%;border:none;border-radius:0;background:transparent;color:var(--w-45)"><div class="pm-i" style="font-size:34px">🗂️</div><div class="pm-l">Old laptop, full lid</div></div></div>
    <div class="story-copy">
      <div class="story-num">01</div>
      <h2>It started with a layout we didn't want to lose</h2>
      <p>The first KeepKase was a fix for a small, real problem. A laptop lid covered in stickers — brands, clubs, a couple of side projects — had become a kind of map of a few years. Then it was time for a new machine, and the only options were bad ones: peel everything off and throw it away, or keep an old laptop around forever just to keep the layout.</p>
      <p>Neither felt right. The stickers weren't disposable, but they weren't permanent either. There was no way to move them, keep them, or come back to them later. So we built one.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="story-block">
  <div class="story-grid reverse">
    <div class="story-copy">
      <div class="story-num">02</div>
      <h2>Expression changes faster than devices</h2>
      <p>You'll keep a laptop for a few years. The things you put on it change a lot faster — a band you stopped listening to, a club you graduated out of, a project that became a job. Protecting a laptop is a solved problem. Keeping the stuff that says something about you, and letting it change without losing it, is not.</p>
      <p>So KeepKase splits the two apart. A thin hardshell border stays on the machine and does the protecting. Two clear polycarbonate sheets snap into it and sandwich your stickers — or a ticket stub, a note, a photo. Nothing sticks to the laptop. The case handles the device; the sheets carry everything else.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="story-media bg-yellow"><div class="placeholder-media" style="height:100%;border:none;border-radius:0;background:transparent"><div class="pm-i" style="font-size:34px">🔄</div><div class="pm-l" style="color:var(--ink-45)">Border stays · sheets swap</div></div></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section bg-paper">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow center" style="display:block;text-align:center;margin-bottom:14px">The three movements</span>
    <div class="pillars">
      <div class="pillar"><div class="pl-k">Preserve</div><h3>Keep the layout</h3><p>Your arrangement stays intact and removable. No adhesive on the anodized finish, nothing scraped off later.</p></div>
      <div class="pillar"><div class="pl-k">Express</div><h3>Swap on a whim</h3><p>Change a design in a minute. Low stakes, no commitment — rearrange as often as you want.</p></div>
      <div class="pillar"><div class="pl-k">Evolve</div><h3>Retire, don't trash</h3><p>When a sheet has run its course, retire it. The next one goes in; the old one doesn't go in the trash.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="story-block">
  <div class="story-grid">
    <div class="story-media bg-coral"><div class="placeholder-media" style="height:100%;border:none;border-radius:0;background:transparent;color:#fff"><div class="pm-i" style="font-size:34px">🖼️</div><div class="pm-l" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,.6)">A wall of retired sheets</div></div></div>
    <div class="story-copy">
      <div class="story-num">03</div>
      <h2>The part you don't see coming</h2>
      <p>A retired sheet doesn't disappear. It goes in a box, or up on a wall. After a while you've got a small stack of them, each one tied to a stretch of time you'd half forgotten.</p>
      <p>The moment people tell us about isn't the unboxing. It's months later — a friend stops at the wall, points at an old club sticker, and asks about it. You end up telling the whole story. That's the thing we're actually building: not a way to decorate a laptop, but a way to change freely because nothing gets lost along the way.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section bg-cream">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow center">
    <div class="story-num" style="text-align:center">04</div>
    <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.8rem,3.4vw,2.8rem);font-weight:900;letter-spacing:-1.5px;margin-bottom:14px">Who it's for, and who it isn't</h2>
    <p class="prose" style="margin:0 auto">KeepKase is for people who treat the outside of a laptop as a personal surface and care how it changes over the years. If you've ever hesitated to put a sticker down because you didn't want to commit to it forever, this was made for you.</p>
    <p class="prose" style="margin:16px auto 0">It's not for everyone, and that's fine. If you see the lid of a laptop as a blank surface to keep clean, or personalization isn't your thing, KeepKase won't change your mind — and we won't try to. We'd rather be the right fit for the people it's for.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section bg-yellow">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="pull-quote"><span class="pq-mark">“</span>Change everything you want to. Keep everything that mattered.<span class="pq-mark">”</span></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section bg-ink">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow center">
    <h2 style="color:#fff;font-size:clamp(1.8rem,3.6vw,3rem);font-weight:900;letter-spacing:-1.8px;line-height:1;margin-bottom:14px">A case becomes a keepsake.</h2>
    <p style="color:var(--w-60);font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;max-width:560px;margin:0 auto 26px">The laptop moves on; the sheets stay with you. Right now we're building it in the open with 100 people — the Alpha is $50, sold at cost, with first pick of colorways and a seat in the Discord where the decisions get made.</p>
    <div class="row gap-3" style="justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap">
      <a href="/products/keepkase-alpha" class="btn btn--yellow btn--lg">Claim an alpha spot — $50 →</a>
      <a href="/pages/community" class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" style="--btn-fg:#fff;border-color:var(--w-30)">See the community</a>
    </div>
    <p style="color:var(--w-45);font-size:13px;margin-top:22px">Designed for what you want to keep — and what you'll outgrow.</p>
  </div>
</section>

